Package: herbivoreTTR
Title: Transparent Models of Herbivore Energetics and Forage Biomass
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Barry", "Brook", email = "barry.brook@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides transparent functional models of herbivore energetics
    and forage biomass.
    The current version converts prescribed dry-matter ingestion through one
    fixed dry-matter-basis metabolizable-energy density into a one-pool
    gut-energy buffer that delays release into a minimal body-energy ledger.
    It can establish a numerical period-24 reference, calculate an hourly
    appetite target from deviations in body and gut energy, constrain realized
    intake with a non-depleting forage-acquisition ceiling, and repeat that
    coupled system over fixed identical days with exact state carry-over.
    Body-energy reserve can also be interpreted as labile reserve tissue and
    total body mass without feeding that derived quantity back into the model.
    A separate isolated forage ledger carries homogeneous standing biomass
    under prescribed growth and background loss with exact stock-flow
    accounting. A linear turnover reference adds constant production and
    proportional background loss around a declared positive equilibrium. A
    pure residual-threshold transformation derives biomass accessible for later
    animal acquisition. The forage subsystem is not yet coupled to the
    herbivore.
